## Data Science Fundamentals Assessment

A comprehensive, professional portfolio assessment designed to validate foundational competencies in data science, Python programming, statistical inference, data preprocessing, and industry workflow best practices.

### 📌 Executive Summary

This repository houses a structured assessment framework built to demonstrate rigorous command over modern data science principles. It bridges theoretical statistical concepts with hands-on technical execution, serving as a key artifact for internship applications, technical interviews, and professional portfolio evaluations.

### 🛠️ Core Competency Modules

The assessment is divided into four robust technical pillars:

Module 1: Python Programming for Data Science

Focuses on core programming paradigms required for data manipulation, automation, and modeling.

Data Structures: Efficient use of lists, dictionaries, tuples, and sets.

Control Flow: Conditional logic, loops, and optimized list comprehensions.

Modular Programming: Writing clean, reusable code, lambda functions, and error handling.

Core Libraries: Introduction to numerical operations via NumPy and tabular data manipulation via Pandas.

Module 2: Statistical Foundations

Provides the mathematical framework required for extracting insights and validating hypotheses.

Descriptive Statistics: Measures of central tendency (mean, median, mode) and dispersion (variance, standard deviation, percentiles).

Probability Theory: Probability distributions, conditional probability, and Bayes' Theorem.

Inferential Statistics: Parametric/non-parametric hypothesis testing ($Z$-test, $T$-test, Chi-Square), $p$-values, confidence intervals, and $A/B$ testing frameworks.

Module 3: Data Types & Preprocessing

Addresses real-world data imperfections to ensure data quality and model readiness.

Data Taxonomy: Working with numerical (continuous/discrete), categorical (nominal/ordinal), datetime, and text data types.

Data Cleansing: Strategies for handling missing data (imputation vs. strategic removal).

Feature Engineering: Scaling, normalization, categorical encoding (One-Hot, Label Encoding), and outlier detection.

Module 4: Industry Best Practices & Workflow

Emphasizes professional engineering standards, collaboration, and ethical considerations.

Version Control: Tracking changes and collaborating effectively using Git and GitHub.

Reproducibility: Workflow documentation, virtual environment management (pip/conda), and clean project structuring.

Ethics & Privacy: Data anonymization, compliance with regulations (GDPR/DPDP), and mitigating algorithmic bias.

🚀 Getting Started & Usage

To explore or execute the assessment deliverables:

Clone the repository:

git clone https://github.com/your-username/data-science-fundamentals-assessment.git
cd data-science-fundamentals-assessment


Set up the virtual environment:

python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate  # On Windows: venv\Scripts\activate


Install dependencies:

pip install -r requirements.txt


